# Sample .stconfig - copy this file to the TOP LEVEL of your source folder
# (the same place a .stignore file lives) and rename it to ".stconfig".
# Prefer a different location? Pass --config <folder> to look there instead.
# Neither? Falls back to the current directory. --no-config ignores the file.
# See "Default options (.stconfig)" in README.md for the full rules.
#
# One "key=value" per line. Blank lines and lines starting with "#" are
# skipped. A command-line option always overrides the matching key here.
# Any key not listed below is an ERROR (an old key names its replacement).

# "source" only matters if this file is found somewhere OTHER than the source
# folder itself (via --config). At the top level of the source folder, drop it.
# source=C:\path\to\ST\Shark

# The project for sync / check events / export: the .sln that `init` created,
# its folder, or a .tsproj.
project=C:\path\to\TwinCAT-projects-root\Shark

# DTE shell: xae (TwinCAT XAE shell) or vs2022.
# shell=xae

# Booleans: "true", "1" or "yes" (any case) are true; anything else is false.
incremental=true
# clean=true

# --- NEVER read from this file ---
# --confirm-delete, --confirm-delete-io, --overwrite, --plc and --yes are
# command-line only, always. The command itself (sync code, check parse, ...)
# chooses the stage; a defaults file cannot.
